WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:06.579
A matrix may have many entries without preserving every input direction. Rank counts independent directions in

00:00:06.579 --> 00:00:12.959
its outputs. The null space contains input changes that the matrix sends to zero, so these

00:00:12.959 --> 00:00:15.750
changes cannot be recovered from the output.

00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:22.810
The second output coordinate is always zero. Although there are two input coordinates, only one independent

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:24.037
output direction survives.

00:00:24.567 --> 00:00:31.064
Substitute this nonzero vector into the map: the first-row contributions cancel, and the second row is

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:31.877
already zero.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:38.655
Will changing the coefficient change the number of lost directions, or only their orientation? Pause here

00:00:38.655 --> 00:00:41.000
and make a prediction before continuing.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:49.660
Rank counts independent output directions. Nullity counts independent input directions sent to zero. For our starting

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:53.440
inputs, Rank: 1. Nullity: 1. Null x-coordinate: -1.

00:00:53.967 --> 00:01:00.658
Adding a null vector to any input leaves its output unchanged. This demonstrates the information loss

00:01:00.658 --> 00:01:01.077
directly.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:07.824
Information loss is a property of the map. A clever inverse algorithm cannot recover a direction

00:01:07.824 --> 00:01:09.380
that every output erased.

